<header><p class="st-kicker">republic · Maritime Southeast Asia</p><h1 class="st-title">Republic of Katagalugan</h1><p class="st-meta">1902 CE – 1906 CE</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">Last revolutionary republic of the Philippine-American War, led by Macario Sakay in the mountains of southern Luzon.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>After the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/united-states">United States</a> declared the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/philippine-american-war">Philippine-American War</a> over in 1902, the former Katipunan member <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/macario-sakay">Macario Sakay</a> refused to accept defeat. In 1902 he revived the name of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/andres-bonifacio">Andres Bonifacio's</a> <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/tagalog-republic">Tagalog Republic</a> and proclaimed the Republic of Katagalugan, with himself as president, in the hills of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rizal-province">Rizal</a> and neighbouring provinces.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The republic had a constitution, a cabinet and a flag, and it organised <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/guerrilla-warfare">guerrilla</a> bands that raided towns in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rizal-province">Rizal</a>, Cavite, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/laguna-province">Laguna</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/batangas">Batangas</a>. American authorities labelled its fighters bandits under the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brigandage-act">Brigandage Act</a> of 1902 and used reconcentration of villagers to cut them off from support.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>In July 1906 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/macario-sakay">Sakay</a> surrendered after the labour leader <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dominador-gomez">Dominador Gomez</a> promised amnesty, but he was arrested, tried for banditry and hanged in 1907. He is now honoured as a Filipino patriot.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="republic, 1902 CE – 1906 CE"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M20 38 L50 20 L80 38 Z"/><path d="M24 42 H76 M24 80 H76"/><path d="M30 44 V78 M43 44 V78 M57 44 V78 M70 44 V78"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">republic</p><p class="st-emblem-region">Maritime Southeast Asia</p><div class="st-span" aria-hidden="true"><span class="st-span-bar" style="left:97.55%;width:1.20%"></span></div><div class="st-span-axis" aria-hidden="true"><span>3000 BCE</span><span>1 CE</span><span>2000</span></div></div><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1902 CE – 1906 CE</dd><dt>Century</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>republic</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>bureaucratic</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Macario Sakay</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Roman Catholicism</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Tagalog</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/philippines">Philippines</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Tagalog Republic (1902-1906)</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1904&amp;focus=republic-of-katagalugan" aria-label="Republic of Katagalugan on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="8065 1765 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Republic of Katagalugan lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M8309 1890h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M8385 2021h0"/><path class="map-dot-ap" d="M8385 2021h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>Location approximate: shown in present-day Philippines. <a href="/atlas?year=1904&amp;focus=republic-of-katagalugan">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>

